# There are two mechanisms to select a topo:
#  1) the command below (`select_topology`) and
#  2) .json sidecar.
# Only the latter can override segment layer assignments (from UI).
# Internally, run_planner does auto layer assignment.
source tracks/tracks4top.buda
add_block b1 0 0 100 100
add_block b2 200 200 300 300
add_bus v[4] b1.o b2.i
add_bus w[4] b2.i b1.o
run_bundler strict
generate_topologies

# a bundle can be pinned to a topo here (B1 -> topo 3):
# select_topologies 1 3
# TopoExp now focuses each bundle's pinned topology (sidecar or script pin)
# consistently — on open, when cycling bundles, and on direct jump.

# here we can create pin in the GUI, too and assign non-default layers on some segments
visualize_topologies

# The sidecar pins a topo with custom layer assignments. If a script
# select_topology(ies) picks a DIFFERENT topo, the script wins and the sidecar's
# layer overrides (which belong to its own topo) are discarded — the planner
# assigns layers automatically. If the script picks the SAME topo as the
# sidecar, the sidecar's custom layer overrides are applied.

run_planner
run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
visualize
